00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.800
Chris Lado, welcome to Lado Files.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.230
Hi, welcome to Lado Files.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:36.230
I have a very exciting guest today.

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:38.230
I'm with John Kiriakou.

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:41.230
He's a former CIA officer, whistleblower and author

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:44.230
who exposed the US government's use of torture

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.230
in its counterterrorism operations.

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.230
As a veteran intelligence officer,

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:52.230
he played a key role in capturing high-profile al-Qaeda members

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.230
before becoming the first US official

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:58.230
to publicly confirm the CIA's waterboarding practices.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:01.230
His revelations led to significant public debate

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:05.230
on ethics in intelligence and government accountability,

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:08.230
ultimately resulting in his own prosecution.

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:11.230
Today's an advocate for whistleblower rights.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:12.230
He's a journalist.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:15.230
He has a show, CIA declassified,

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:18.230
and he's a vocal critic of governmental overreach.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.230
Thank you, John, for being here.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.230
How are you doing today, sir?

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:21.230
Thanks for having me.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:23.230
Doing well, thanks.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:24.230
Okay, amazing.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:27.230
I was happy to be on your CIA declassified show.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:29.230
We'll show a teaser later on in the show.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:34.230
But on that, you explained about your own personal UAP experience.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.230
Can you tell us about that?

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:37.230
My audience would love to hear it.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:38.230
Sure.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:41.230
When I was 17 years old,

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:45.230
my mom and dad bought a restaurant in a nearby town.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:47.230
We lived in Newcastle, Pennsylvania,

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:49.230
which is about an hour north of Pittsburgh.

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:51.230
It's a very rural area.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.230
They bought a restaurant in Sharon, Pennsylvania.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:55.230
It was 20 miles away.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:58.230
And so to get from Newcastle to Sharon,

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:00.230
you have to drive through Amish country.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:03.230
And it's very, very dark in Amish country

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:06.230
because the Amish don't use any electricity.

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:10.230
So my dad and I, on the weekends, worked the midnight shift.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:11.230
I was a short order cook,

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:14.230
and of course he was there to manage the restaurant.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:18.230
So we left our house on a Friday night.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:19.230
It was at 10 o'clock.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:22.230
Figure we'll get there at 10 30 to start working at 11.

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:27.230
And we're in Amish country, very, very dark again.

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:28.230
And as we're driving,

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:32.230
we see this brilliant flash of white light.

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:34.230
And we both looked up into the sky

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:38.230
and there's a second flash and then a third flash.

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:42.230
And then this orange trapezoid lit up

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:46.230
and just hovered in the sky.

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:50.230
We pulled the car over and got out.

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:53.230
So the thing hovered there for long enough

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:55.230
for us to get out of the car.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.230
And we're standing there just staring at it.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.230
Without saying anything,

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:03.230
a man pulls up behind us and gets out and he says,

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:05.230
what the heck is that?

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:07.230
And my dad said, I don't know.

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:12.230
And then it just took off at a fantastic speed.

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:15.230
Unlike anything I've seen,

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:18.230
or I had seen before or have seen since,

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:21.230
I mean, it just, it went like that.

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:23.230
Fantastic speed.

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:26.230
And we just stood there looking in the sky.

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:28.230
And then we got back into the car,

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:30.230
started driving again.

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:32.230
And I said to my father,

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:34.230
should we call somebody?

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:37.230
Should we like call the cops or something?

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:39.230
And he said to say what,

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:42.230
we saw UFO and it flew away.

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:44.230
People will think we're crazy.

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:46.230
And so we didn't say anything.

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:48.230
I told my mom the next morning.

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:50.230
She believed us, of course.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:52.230
My dad said exactly the same thing that I did.

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:56.230
And I'll tell you, for weeks after that,

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:59.230
my eyes were just glued into the night sky,

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:03.230
hoping that I could see it again or something again.

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:07.230
And that was, you know, 43 years ago.

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:11.230
And I've never seen anything like that since.

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:13.230
That's an amazing story.

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:15.230
And you said no sound, right?

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:17.230
No sound at all.

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:19.230
And it just hovered.

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:22.230
And it wasn't terribly far away.

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:25.230
I'm going to say it was hovering at,

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:28.230
I don't know, 2,000 feet,

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:31.230
3,000 feet, maybe 3,000 feet.

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:34.230
And not making any sound at all,

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:35.230
just hovering there.

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:36.230
And I should add too.

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:39.230
So it's in this trapezoidal,

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:41.230
my fingers can't do it,

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:44.230
trapezoidal shape.

00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:49.230
And in the four corners of it were bright glowing orange lights

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:52.230
to the point where the orange lights were so bright

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:56.230
that they illuminated the rest of whatever it was.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:07:00.230
And you know, over the years I've said to myself,

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:01.230
maybe it was a balloon.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.230
No, of course it's not a balloon

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:08.230
because of the speed with which it took off like that.

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:10.230
And it wasn't just floating there

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:13.230
and then it just kind of casually floated away

00:07:13.230 --> 00:07:15.230
like a balloon might.

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:18.230
There's a small municipal airport.

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:22.230
Oh, just three or four miles away.

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:24.230
But it closes at sunset.

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:27.230
And so it wasn't that.

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:29.230
And I honestly,

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:34.230
I don't have any explanation for what it was

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:38.230
other than it was unexplained.

00:07:38.230 --> 00:07:41.230
Any idea how large it was or how big it was?

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:43.230
I know it's hard to tell at distance.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:47.230
Yeah, hard to tell, but I'm going to say

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:55.630
I'm going to say it was probably 25 or 30 feet across.

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:59.630
Big, bigger than, you know, a Cessna.

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:03.630
It was at that airport that I learned to fly years later.

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:05.630
So comparing it to a Cessna.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:12.940
Yeah, it was two or three, two and a half, three times the size.

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:14.940
Did you talk to your father later on,

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:17.940
like later in your life about it?

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:19.940
Yeah, I sure did.

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:21.940
But it was always one of us saying,

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:26.940
remember that thing we saw up in the sky back in in 82?

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:30.940
Like, well, how can I forget that thing we saw up in the sky in 82?

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:32.940
Yeah, I remember it.

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:35.940
And then, you know, because I had seen something,

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.940
I immediately took an interest.

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:42.940
And as I mentioned to you on, on the CIA to classified,

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:46.940
Jimmy Carter saw something that was unexplained and went so far

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:50.940
as to file a police report saying that he had seen this

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:52.940
thing hovering in the sky.

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:55.940
But he said that what he saw was buzzing.

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:58.940
He admitted a buzz that he could hear.

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:01.940
But if the president of the United States is seeing, you know,

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:05.940
things in the sky, then, you know, I don't feel so alone.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:06.940
Yeah.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:08.940
When, when is the first time you actually talked about it?

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:10.940
Did you feel the stigma?

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.940
You know, did you feel a need to keep quiet about this?

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:14.940
I did.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:15.940
I did because I didn't,

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:18.940
I didn't want people to think I was crazy or making something up.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:20.940
And I tell you what, over the years I've,

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:23.940
I've thought about it and I've, I've thought, you know,

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:26.940
my goodness, my dad was there and my dad saw it because my father

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:30.940
was, you know, this seriously a pillar of the community.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:35.940
When he died, it was on the front page of the local paper.

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:38.940
He was that kind of a pillar of the community.

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:45.800
And so if Chris Kiriakou saw it, then something was up there.

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:47.800
And did he ever talk about it?

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:48.800
No.

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:49.800
Publicly.

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:50.800
No, never.

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:52.800
Just to me.

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:56.800
And like I say, it was, it was always remember that thing we saw up in

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:58.800
the sky in 82.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:02.100
Yeah.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.100
Have you seen anything since then?

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:06.100
No, nothing even remotely close.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:10.100
But I've mentioned this a couple of times to friends, close friends

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:12.100
and relatives.

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:16.100
And I've been surprised at how many people have seen things that

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:18.100
they just have not been able to explain.

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:24.100
I mentioned to you on CIA to classified that I'm very close to

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:27.100
a, to a cousin, a second cousin.

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:32.100
He's older than I am 14, 15 years older than I am.

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:36.100
And his father owned a restaurant too here in, in Alexandria,

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:37.100
Virginia.

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:41.100
And so when I was a kid, I used to come down here, stay with

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:43.100
them, hang out at the restaurant.

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:46.100
And he had a friend who was an Air Force pilot.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:52.100
And he told me once that he saw something, some sort of

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:56.100
craft dive straight down into the water.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:59.100
Off the coast of Virginia Beach, Virginia.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:03.100
And then seconds later come straight up out of the water and

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:04.100
fly away.

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:06.100
And I said, what in the world do you think that was?

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:09.100
And he said, we're not supposed to use the words flying saucer,

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:13.100
but it looked like a flying saucer going down to get a drink.

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:15.100
That's what it looked like.

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:17.100
And that's always stuck with me as well.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:21.100
And again, this isn't just some nut that you sit next to

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:22.100
in a bar.

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:26.100
This is an Air Force pilot, a fighter pilot, right?

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:28.100
These are the best of the best.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:31.100
They're the guys who have gone through the most extensive

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:35.100
training and, you know, to be able to handle a craft like

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:36.100
that.

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:40.100
And if he says that he saw something like that, I believe

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:41.100
him.

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:44.100
It's interesting too because the coast of Virginia,

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:47.100
that's basically where Ryan Graves, you know, his

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:50.100
four ship video, the gimbal.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:51.100
That's right.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:52.100
UAP video.

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:54.100
And they've seen many other sightings.

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:57.100
They said almost daily sightings of these strange objects,

00:11:57.100 --> 00:12:00.100
you know, a dark cube inside of a sphere, some sort of

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:01.100
clear sphere.

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:03.100
So it's interesting off the coast of Virginia.

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:07.100
And, you know, it makes me think too, whatever these

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:12.100
are, do they congregate around air bases?

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:16.100
Or is it because we have air bases and we have

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:20.100
pilots and people trained in this kind of thing that we

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:22.100
see them there more frequently?

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:24.800
I'm not sure.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:27.800
I think, yeah, we don't know, you know, because the

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:30.800
data certainly comes from where our military aircraft

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:33.800
are flying, or at least from Aero, you know, the data

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:36.800
they released was basically all of our training areas.

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:38.800
So it could be where we're looking.

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:41.800
Maybe that's why our nuclear sites have so much

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:42.800
surveillance.

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:44.800
You know, maybe that's why we're seeing them or

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:47.800
our military aircraft are out there actually seeing

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:48.800
these things.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.800
It could be, I guess, everywhere, but we're just not

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:52.800
